From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: keep the noise floor when a channel is entered

While a phy has no operating channel (hostapd ACS at start), every
channel the scan enters is a channel other than the main one, and
__mt76_set_channel() clears its whole channel state. The noise floor
is cleared with the counters, so a survey dump that arrives while the
phy sits on the channel it has just entered reports no noise for it.
hostapd then logs "Survey for freq 2412 is missing noise floor" for
the channel the scan starts and parks on, and ACS discards it.

The counters restart with every visit; the noise floor is an average
that the next update continues, so keep it across the clear. When the
driver has no counts yet, mt7915_update_channel() must not replace the
floor that the state holds with none.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1157,8 +1157,17 @@
 	if (!offchannel)
 		phy->main_chandef = *chandef;
 
-	if (chandef->chan != phy->main_chandef.chan)
+	if (chandef->chan != phy->main_chandef.chan) {
+		/* the counters restart with every visit, the noise floor is
+		 * an average that the next update continues: without it the
+		 * channel that has just been entered (a survey dump during a
+		 * scan, hostapd ACS) has no noise at all
+		 */
+		s8 noise = phy->chan_state->noise;
+
 		memset(phy->chan_state, 0, sizeof(*phy->chan_state));
+		phy->chan_state->noise = noise;
+	}
 
 	ret = dev->drv->set_channel(phy);
 
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1231,7 +1231,11 @@
 	else if (nf)
 		phy->noise += nf - (phy->noise >> 4);
 
-	state->noise = -(phy->noise >> 4);
+	/* no counts and no average yet: keep the floor that the channel state
+	 * holds instead of reporting none
+	 */
+	if (phy->noise)
+		state->noise = -(phy->noise >> 4);
 }
 
 static bool
